INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('4329c7fe-a576-4071-963b-5533bccd4373','md-gollwitzer-implementation-intentions-application-to-ai-curriculum-and-task-design','Application to AI Curriculum and Task Design

### Task-Level Implementation Intentions
Every assigned task should anchor to an environmental cue from the user''s own routine. The goal intake process should capture: when does the user typically study? Where? What happens immediately before?

Example output from intake: "You mentioned you study after dinner. Implementation: ''''When dinner is done and dishes are cleared, I will open [app] and start today''''s task — even if only for 10 minutes.''''"

### The TimeConstraint Stone and If-Then Fallbacks
For users with TimeConstraint stones, every task needs an explicit micro-session implementation intention as a fallback:
"If I only have 5-10 minutes, I will do [specific micro-version of today''''s task]."

This converts a potential skip (decision: can I do the full task? No. Skip.) into a partial completion (decision: already made — do the micro version automatically).

### Inconsistency Stone: Never-Miss-Twice Coping Plan
For users with Inconsistency stones, the implementation intention structure:
"If I miss a day, I will do tomorrow''''s task within 30 minutes of waking, regardless of how I feel."

This prevents the typical two-day gap that precedes full habit abandonment. The coping plan activates automatically rather than requiring motivational recovery.

### Weekly Review Implementation Intentions
Research shows implementation intentions for review sessions are even more effective than for practice sessions because reviews feel less intrinsically motivating. Pre-specifying when/where/how to review closes the most likely drop-off point in a spaced repetition curriculum.','gollwitzer-implementation-intentions','{"habit-formation"}','{"application","curriculum","task","design","task-level","implementation","intentions","every","assigned","anchor","environmental","user''s","routine","goal","intake"}','[0.08789998,-0.06421958,0.20216332,0.03402295,-0.01896297,-0.01072169,-0.09712716,0.03284103,0.01369196,-0.13737135,-0.08367511,-0.05029475,-0.05992183,0.03189592,0.1489703,0.09147003,0.02270481,0.05208533,0.01245449,-0.05468123,-0.05846393,-0.02267964,-0.03545671,0.14353833,-0.06041204,-0.00648178,-0.01347107,-0.03134339,0.03572085,-0.0491082,0.01747211,-0.02619349,-0.0505745,0.00787045,0.00709737,0.01551683,0.06428257,0.01616924,0.09614629,0.04348257,-0.01595053,0.02930366,-0.02700345,0.06212961,0.01698164,0.03128079,-0.01504438,0.024203,0.05890297,-0.06087789,0.04816966,0.12933172,-0.0244466,-0.00755348,0.0073876,0.06047875,0.06523095,0.01374691,-0.0307983,0.01558271,-0.04222328,-0.10312347,0.03280078,-0.08402356,-0.06524374,-0.02766141,0.02654163,-0.00603328,-0.06629474,-0.05612235,0.08033437,-0.02136151,-0.00559632,0.08371107,-0.01954915,0.00257084,-0.04350305,0.02494573,-0.00580154,0.01126924,-0.02045885,-0.05658451,0.05667064,0.03883313,-0.00650546,-0.00571955,-0.12799631,-0.00894434,-0.028333,-0.02406108,-0.06707879,-0.0396879,-0.05329545,-0.0391717,0.0702072,-0.08890893,-0.00094768,0.01163842,-0.03368131,0.0040976,-0.01698965,0.01218774,0.01905762,-0.0289277,0.01112719,-0.03304018,0.06334748,0.01489339,-0.07304253,-0.0263421,-0.02819454,-0.00616476,0.05649636,0.01737892,0.06874382,0.05859025,0.00047001,0.01611877,0.04485539,0.1033773,0.02742152,-0.01472348,-0.01062458,0.00027851,-0.01577344,0.01942546,-0.02714929,0.07588543,0.00392414,-0.00154011,-0.0056224