INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('e2111014-c1ca-4532-a6db-cb5ad8b7bff3','md-self-efficacy-bandura-the-four-sources-of-self-efficacy','The Four Sources of Self-Efficacy

### 1. Mastery Experiences (Strongest Source — ~60% of variance)
Direct personal success is the most powerful builder of self-efficacy. Each success raises the efficacy ceiling; each failure, if attributed internally, lowers it.

Critical nuance: Easy successes do not build robust efficacy. Successes achieved through moderate challenge and persistence build stronger, more resilient efficacy than outcomes that required no effort. This is the research basis for "desirable difficulty" in learning.

Coaching implication: Early sprints should be calibrated so that the person succeeds at slightly challenging versions of the target behavior — not trivially easy, not overwhelming. The stretch zone, not the panic zone.

### 2. Vicarious Experiences (Social Modeling — ~20% of variance)
Observing similar others succeed raises self-efficacy. The more similar the model to the observer, the stronger the effect. "If they can do it, I can do it."

The key word is similar: watching elite athletes does not raise self-efficacy for fitness beginners. Watching someone at the same starting point succeed is what matters.

Coaching implication: Social proof from people at a similar starting level is more motivating than aspirational examples. Show "someone like you" succeeding.

### 3. Verbal Persuasion (Encouragement — ~10% of variance)
Being told you are capable of something raises efficacy modestly. The source must be credible and specific to matter. Credible: the person respects the source. Specific: "You handled that well because..." not "You''''re great."

Important limitation: Persuasion raises efficacy less than mastery experiences, and can backfire if the person is subsequently challenged and fails — it raises expectations without providing actual capability.

### 4. Physiological and Emotional States (~10% of variance)
Physical arousal, stress, fatigue, and mood all affect efficacy appraisals. A person who feels anxious before a task interprets that arousal as evidence of low ability. A person who feels calm interprets the same physiological state as energized readiness.

Coaching implication: Pre-task ritual design matters. Helping users reinterpret arousal ("that nervousness is energy") can shift efficacy without any change in actual ability.','self-efficacy-bandura','{"habit-formation"}','{"four","sources","self-efficacy","mastery","experiences","strongest","source","variance","direct","personal","success","most","powerful","builder","each"}','[0.04975959,-0.01046829,0.01015735,-0.07809037,-0.02236783,-0.01413777,-0.05966306,0.04000759,0.01271519,-0.06019275,-0.0486992,-0.06811206,0.00525516,-0.02926352,0.16128454,0.13599108,-0.06893252,-0.00200646,0.0152836,-0.04274246,-0.07358408,0.0102717,0.04321997,0.07350007,-0.02482031,-0.0959386,-0.01265697,-0.05113546,-0.13038062,-0.07692064,0.02610007,-0.00197089,0.02159756,0.18057004,0.02420294,-0.0499344,0.01021627,0.04129944,-0.03658354,0.02698643,-0.0210479,0.0520058,0.0498811,0.00108633,0.05021863,0.08842006,0.07023592,-0.05509606,-0.02317099,-0.05286901,-0.01474634,-0.01677812,-0.01627152,0.06711701,-0.07335405,-0.02269194,-0.03525561,-0.00461427,0.03482428,-0.0439416,0.02325774,-0.00444616,-0.10502463,0.05594623,-0.03217823,-0.02545397,0.01439046,-0.01889013,-0.05568577,0.04522244,-0.02699266,-0.01506879,-0.0267493,-0.03373858,-0.02654836,0.01937908,0.01960464,-0.10711845,0.07782253,-0.00151123,-0.06090457,0.01287177,0.00691534,-0.01268219,0.01816923,-0.0362219,-0.0564674,0.00634835,0.02963027,0.00871835,-0.0719991,-0.04367096,-0.09494411,-0.09604451,0.00199644,-0.01705391,0.04389957,-0.01728362,0.05955077,0.03292907,-0.01921106,0.05925402,-0.05872792,0.03709936,-0.02544557,0.03496328,-0.021791,-0.04996954,-0.06394553,0.0300744,-0.01717756,0.0785034,-0.00035152,-0.04253186,-0.00536926,-0.02737141,0.00485174,-0.04243763,0.01894918,0.04025705,-0.00012531,0.02917836,-0.00246489,0.08663013,0.01639298,0.03228926,0.00269563,0.00206958,-0.00521179,0.0151952,-0.0306306,-0.01641947,0.02981401,-0.01478118,0.00394401,0.07840061,0.01477859,-0.03784619,-0.00268794,0.02155043,-0.03962851,0.06494