INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('d30c4692-ee6b-4b97-b68b-a3aeb9a5fad1','md-consistency-building-reducing-session-startup-friction','Reducing Session Startup Friction

The highest-risk moment for inconsistent learners is the transition from "not doing" to "doing."

Friction reduction tactics:
- Prepare the session environment the night before
- Have a "launch sequence": same 3 actions that precede every session (e.g., make tea, open app, start timer)
- Commitment devices: sign up for a class, pay for a session in advance, tell someone
