INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('edb0c471-0e5d-4ab1-ac37-2dba712002df','md-language-learning-phase-1-core-vocabulary-and-sound-system-weeks-1-6','Phase 1: Core Vocabulary and Sound System (Weeks 1–6)

The fastest path to conversational ability is vocabulary frequency. The top 1000 words of any language cover 85% of everyday speech. Learn these first, not grammar rules.

Daily template: 15 min Anki flashcard review (spaced repetition) + 20 min new input (audio or reading) + 10 min output (speaking or writing).

Week 1–2: Phonetics and survival phrases
- Learn the sound system — every phoneme in the target language
- 50 survival phrases: greetings, numbers 1–100, days, months, colors
- Start Anki deck: add 10 new cards per day, review all due cards
- Milestone: Pronounce 50 words and be understood by a native speaker (test via iTalki or HiNative)

Week 3–4: Core vocabulary acceleration
- Top 300 frequency words — Anki only, no grammar books yet
- Listen to beginner podcasts (Language Transfer, Pimsleur) for 20 min per day
- Milestone: Recognize 200+ words by ear in native audio — no translation needed

Week 5–6: Basic sentence construction
- Learn subject-verb-object patterns. 5 verb tenses maximum.
- Write 10 sentences per day about your real life (what you did, plan to do, like/dislike)
- Start shadowing: replay native audio sentence by sentence, mimic intonation
- Milestone: Write a 5-sentence paragraph about your day. Correct it with a tutor.

Common pitfalls: Spending Phase 1 studying grammar tables instead of acquiring vocabulary. Grammar rules are patterns — acquire them through exposure, not memorization.','Coheren Domain KB — Language Learning','{"skill-progression","cognitive"}','{"phase","core","vocabulary","sound","system","weeks","fastest","path","conversational","ability","frequency","1000","words","language","cover"}','[0.09688396,-0.0855066,0.12520078,0.00561295,0.05980816,-0.01639117,-0.11490785,0.05520092,0.02545035,-0.18192102,-0.06229563,-0.12149473,0.01606491,0.0352377,0.02964262,-0.00460908,-0.01369514,-0.04962163,-0.08704092,0.03010668,-0.09664678,0.02786435,-0.0417357,0.02483105,0.00774567,-0.06310395,0.05876649,-0.03745717,-0.0544251,-0.05239964,-0.03561072,-0.03810069,-0.11479126,0.03715395,-0.01900636,-0.02169295,0.07222227,0.02993519,0.03126871,0.05915974,0.05624699,0.01395878,-0.01961291,0.11875279,0.027496,0.02408237,0.10471199,0.01489349,0.08129641,0.00572854,0.02039437,0.11604741,-0.04874732,0.04656239,-0.01728045,0.05569487,0.03930104,0.00175401,0.01324463,0.02005545,-0.02591991,0.08323992,-0.02823466,0.03661208,-0.05348327,-0.04005108,-0.0551484,-0.0135501,-0.02919818,-0.01348385,0.09763039,-0.03988082,0.01907234,0.05047702,-0.01782503,0.03339375,0.01548905,0.05753037,0.03826768,0.00033126,-0.01250046,-0.00010658,0.06493326,0.06796141,0.08984841,-0.07542507,-0.02309413,0.00333869,0.00841869,0.00508838,-0.05122134,-0.05728591,0.0273831,0.02526042,-0.0288321,0.00351376,-0.02338121,-0.01072321,0.00888549,-0.01631634,0.0238408,-0.01228926,0.04862748,-0.0323303,0.01364957,-0.06071473,0.01218644,0.03329537,0.03605875,-0.05816502,0.01245832,0.0408068,0.03855315,-0.04369126,0.02811531,0.06100062,0.01974953,-0.01275282,0.02242422,-0.0346186,-0.03483524,-0.08165145,-0.04616491,-0.00903301,0.02910165,0.0202083,-0.08470789,0.03672087,0.03503827,0.02955329,-0.02288319,0.06283394,-0.04323095,0.03853741,0.04525555,0.03229852,-0.03290489,-0.05995131,0.00711413,0.05487698,0.05000907,0.0203905