INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('59f242fe-1bc3-4754-bf11-c1496f3d9b79','md-programming-phase-1-core-mechanics-weeks-1-4','Phase 1: Core Mechanics (Weeks 1–4)

Absolute beginners must build mental models before writing code. The sequence matters: variables and types → control flow → functions → basic data structures. Skipping order creates gaps that become bugs.

Daily template: 20 min concept study (read/watch) + 25 min practice problems (write code, not copy-paste).

Week 1–2 focus: Variables, data types, conditionals, loops
- Day 1–3: Variables, strings, numbers, booleans — write 5 small programs that print output
- Day 4–7: if/else chains — write a number guessing game from scratch
- Day 8–10: for and while loops — FizzBuzz, count-down timers, sum calculators
- Day 11–14: Combine all three — build a CLI quiz with 5 questions

Milestone: Solve 15 HackerRank Easy problems without looking at solutions. If you need hints, you haven''t consolidated yet — spend one more week.

Week 3–4 focus: Functions and basic data structures
- Day 15–17: Functions — parameters, return values, scope. Refactor your quiz into functions.
- Day 18–21: Arrays — iteration, map/filter/reduce patterns. Build a student grade calculator.
- Day 22–24: Objects/dictionaries — model real things (user profile, shopping cart item).
- Day 25–28: Mini-project: Build a CLI todo app (add, remove, list, mark done).

Milestone: CLI todo app working with all 4 commands. Code is readable without comments.

Common pitfalls: Watching tutorials without writing code (tutorial hell), skipping to OOP before functions are solid, naming variables "x" and "temp" (use descriptive names from day 1).','Coheren Domain KB — Programming','{"skill-progression","cognitive"}','{"phase","core","mechanics","weeks","absolute","beginners","must","build","mental","models","before","writing","code","sequence","matters"}','[0.07555147,-0.00562161,0.1610835,0.08301914,0.00421282,-0.01691893,-0.08385848,-0.05159734,-0.0180666,-0.0901194,-0.04337692,-0.11670528,-0.01854446,0.05800182,0.01037544,0.03721853,0.05217136,0.08273631,-0.02642262,0.01510355,-0.14580722,0.0071976,-0.0008663,0.1372823,0.02132563,-0.07018288,-0.04027228,-0.03570792,-0.08138048,0.01969554,0.10761026,0.06462198,-0.06597374,0.04112613,-0.01865456,-0.00403809,0.0694011,0.07192583,0.087313,-0.0180963,0.01145386,0.01701337,-0.02732614,0.05973074,-0.02847042,0.00632176,0.08754376,-0.01596036,0.02695623,-0.08127903,-0.01860365,0.0897984,-0.01036688,-0.02718692,0.01347242,0.03904955,0.01185778,-0.05070132,-0.02469786,0.0251771,-0.02797526,0.05175178,0.04453824,-0.00954315,-0.07826763,-0.05457442,-0.05539875,0.0803339,-0.06458148,0.00898905,0.0798221,-0.03084608,0.0714194,0.02813763,-0.00634845,-0.01160856,0.02797718,0.03317989,-0.0654167,0.03016733,-0.03836642,0.03601367,0.06739506,0.01544681,0.01517499,-0.04732722,-0.07769494,0.07456122,-0.05350068,-0.03633315,-0.05681609,0.02281564,0.07369151,-0.05643829,0.01406504,0.02109884,0.02660136,0.01948151,-0.04975466,0.03249742,0.0402076,0.05655413,-0.00866262,-0.06513988,0.07238659,-0.033631,0.05635528,0.00799565,0.00717501,-0.0566556,-0.0037687,-0.00701617,0.05591669,0.01500847,0.03518221,0.11493428,0.004133,-0.03209136,-0.03545913,0.06917281,-0.03638338,0.05406042,0.04118099,-0.00896332,0.00435899,-0.02458186,-0.05390776,0.02258638,0.00733891,-0.01287748,-0.00119819,0.04467455,0.00171998,0.05678595,-0.04876613,0.0170891,-0.03424808,-0.05166546,0.01023167,0.02360321,0.06660875,-0.02261