INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('07afc8b1-800a-4606-9688-dc9960055b9b','md-budgeting-phase-1-financial-visibility-weeks-1-3','Phase 1: Financial Visibility (Weeks 1–3)

You cannot manage what you cannot see. Most people have no accurate picture of their spending — they guess, and the guess is always lower than reality.

Net worth calculation (Day 1):
- Assets: checking, savings, investments, property value, car value
- Liabilities: mortgage balance, auto loan, student loans, credit card balances, personal loans
- Net worth = Assets - Liabilities
- Track this number monthly. The direction matters, not the number.

Income and spending audit:
- Download 3 months of bank and credit card statements
- Categorize every transaction (most banks auto-categorize — review accuracy)
- Categories: Housing, Transport, Food (grocery separate from dining out), Entertainment, Subscriptions, Health, Clothing, Miscellaneous
- No judgment in this phase — only visibility

Surprise expenses identification:
- Annual expenses that catch people off-guard: car registration, insurance renewals, holiday gifts, vacations, medical deductibles
- Divide each by 12 and treat as monthly budget line items
- These are NOT emergencies — they''re predictable irregular expenses

Milestone: Know exactly where last month''s money went, categorized, to within 5%. Find one subscription you forgot you had.','Coheren Domain KB — Budgeting','{"skill-progression","financial"}','{"phase","financial","visibility","weeks","cannot","manage","what","most","people","accurate","picture","spending","guess","always","lower"}','[-0.00657791,-0.03307851,0.03419568,0.06881177,-0.01084779,0.02483321,-0.03448258,0.01285654,0.03886409,-0.04450405,-0.090139,-0.02662021,-0.02610601,0.08441465,0.00431664,0.00443477,0.03372915,0.10193001,0.16608237,-0.08643411,-0.06966536,-0.06595092,0.00294809,0.02226261,-0.11219747,-0.05749836,-0.14665866,0.00018499,-0.06529412,-0.1187497,0.14131054,-0.09515841,-0.12891427,0.03920715,-0.07502667,-0.03691565,0.01423988,0.07415979,0.06209402,0.08725165,0.06186767,0.05361886,-0.00636203,0.01785635,-0.02912575,-0.026549,0.10484096,0.03761893,-0.01097811,-0.05595774,-0.04166827,0.07676436,-0.11284562,0.02082235,-0.11218873,0.03911921,-0.04072131,0.02589057,-0.06415713,-0.03360588,-0.00281369,0.01533645,0.01672458,0.08209214,-0.00546004,-0.01360377,0.01342398,0.02752714,-0.04071098,0.08734865,0.05129353,-0.02241645,0.0572824,0.05782326,0.0276075,0.0239406,0.06169533,-0.06531145,0.00596798,0.00512719,-0.03570671,0.01980128,0.07200998,0.05128424,0.0144748,0.04046179,-0.05741719,-0.00804559,-0.01008467,-0.02223761,-0.0486851,0.00663092,-0.03194692,0.02667448,0.02637845,0.00268451,-0.020346,0.0058037,-0.02282006,0.00278578,0.07511786,-0.01955618,0.01755525,-0.04627435,0.03781499,-0.00869621,-0.006948,-0.04699516,0.06193202,-0.08127191,-0.01324057,0.04730016,0.01851055,-0.0319944,-0.03899235,0.05596538,0.02174342,-0.04034377,-0.0686813,0.00139568,0.04277202,-0.01797941,0.1087688,-0.0223654,0.02526108,-0.03266903,-0.06078076,-0.00681965,0.04008326,0.02150056,-0.02498199,0.02362003,0.00670683,0.0580171,-0.01744469,0.02698253,0.0260379,-0.03260601,0.01577066,0.01400174,-0.02343524,0.0213323,0.03541943,0.02430116,-0.05443421,0.01969407,-0.0391724