INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('dc3fb2a7-c616-455e-af34-e57f5b3a006e','md-video-content-phase-1-equipment-process-and-first-videos-weeks-1','Phase 1: Equipment, Process, and First Videos (Weeks 1–4)

The biggest barrier to starting a YouTube channel is gear perfectionism. The camera on a 2021+ smartphone is good enough. Most successful channels started with equipment far below modern smartphones.

Minimum viable setup:
- Camera: smartphone or webcam (both acceptable)
- Microphone: $30-50 USB condenser (Blue Snowball or similar) — audio matters more than video quality
- Lighting: face a window (natural light) or one ring light ($30)
- Editing: CapCut (free, phone or desktop), DaVinci Resolve (free, desktop), iMovie (free, Mac)

Video is a craft with five learnable sub-skills:
1. On-camera presence (scripting, delivery, energy)
2. Camera operation (framing, focus, exposure)
3. Audio quality (room acoustics, mic placement)
4. Editing (pacing, cuts, graphics, music)
5. Thumbnails and titles (click-through rate optimization)

Week 1–2: Production fundamentals
- Script your first 3 videos completely (scripting reduces on-camera anxiety)
- Record each one — do not stop and restart when you make mistakes, keep recording
- Edit the best version — you will hate watching yourself. Do it anyway.
- Milestone: 3 complete videos from script to final edit. Not published — just completed.

Week 3–4: First publication and feedback
- Publish your first video — to YouTube (unlisted or public)
- Watch your analytics: audience retention graph (where do viewers drop off?) is the most important metric
- Retention drop-offs tell you where you lost the audience — this is your editing and scripting feedback
- Milestone: First video published. Audience retention graph reviewed.','Coheren Domain KB — Video Content','{"skill-progression","creative"}','{"phase","equipment","process","first","videos","weeks","biggest","barrier","starting","youtube","channel","gear","perfectionism","camera","2021"}','[0.0728005,-0.00916198,0.10608467,0.00238511,0.03440405,0.03309714,-0.09066484,0.04078805,-0.07227603,-0.09361006,-0.00655615,-0.04721944,0.08107057,0.01467089,0.01377622,-0.01757023,0.01557383,0.08116262,0.10062536,-0.04089756,-0.06956001,-0.06915747,-0.01797832,0.05406627,0.0224548,-0.13456456,-0.05627504,0.00387325,-0.05830951,-0.03390258,-0.07130499,-0.00396323,-0.07241403,0.06011016,-0.02005031,-0.13869184,-0.02181715,0.15329629,-0.01428683,-0.00229715,0.00692964,-0.00407874,0.06416979,-0.00963133,-0.00348126,-0.0902755,0.0494591,0.0472788,0.01336282,-0.03358311,-0.05372884,0.0013351,-0.03198169,-0.04306581,-0.00604131,0.06138,0.01360085,-0.00655498,0.02839861,-0.05242887,-0.13654245,0.03080344,0.01825392,0.03432128,-0.0434064,-0.05887645,-0.04430362,0.01793423,-0.03766824,0.0489089,0.07570864,-0.07494964,-0.01285338,-0.00768813,0.01325908,0.03329322,0.02257633,-0.00746818,0.01078114,-0.03414888,-0.0101224,-0.04917831,0.04093402,0.0376779,0.08311142,0.00363858,-0.06690527,0.05174022,0.03073781,0.03135743,-0.00385426,0.01136566,0.01219868,-0.01805955,0.01125341,-0.05907941,0.02647986,-0.00078858,-0.04203586,0.01320543,0.01969608,0.01510462,0.0040995,-0.00796,0.03337086,0.04356649,0.07099686,0.01547135,0.08161363,0.00815639,-0.00528471,0.05702548,-0.11659043,-0.07122186,-0.01707078,0.05583819,0.03815508,-0.08308219,-0.02578601,0.02996509,-0.04264292,-0.03553553,0.01217249,-0.00099143,0.07481603,0.01771511,-0.05522287,-0.04267641,-0.02511261,0.05257845,-0.0085789,0.01181443,-0.05293656,0.03361197,-0.02049264,0.04754973,-0.04417292,-0.040356,-0.01219415,0.03435674,0.05638649,-0.00215707,0.00910756,-0.01536356,-0.03281867,-0.00628238,-0.00052975,0.01565882,-0.00849182,0.02057268