INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('47d89e5a-f297-43e6-b1c8-fb0b80d78e2c','md-investing-beginner-phase-1-financial-foundations-weeks-1-4','Phase 1: Financial Foundations (Weeks 1–4)

No investment strategy works on top of a broken financial foundation. Sequence matters: emergency fund → debt elimination → investment basics.

Emergency fund first:
- 3-6 months of essential expenses in a high-yield savings account
- No investments until this exists — a market dip can''t force you to sell if you have cash reserves
- HYSA target yield: Fed funds rate - 0.5% (check current rates, not a fixed number)

Debt priority:
- High-interest debt (>7% APR): pay off before investing — guaranteed 7%+ return
- Student loans / mortgage (<5% APR): can invest alongside repayment
- Debt avalanche: pay minimums on all, then extra payments to highest-APR debt first

Core investment concepts (learn before touching money):
- Compound interest: $1000 at 7% for 30 years = $7,612. Time is the only variable you can''t buy back.
- Inflation: your cash loses purchasing power at ~3% per year — keeping everything in savings has a guaranteed cost
- Risk/return tradeoff: higher expected returns require tolerating larger price swings
- Diversification: not putting eggs in one basket — but also not spreading so thin nothing matters

Paper trading before real money:
- Open a paper trading account (TD Ameritrade thinkorswim, Investopedia Stock Simulator)
- Execute all planned trades in simulation for 4 weeks before committing real money
- Goal: learn the mechanics, not generate returns

Milestone: Emergency fund funded. Paper trading account opened. Core concepts can be explained to a friend.','Coheren Domain KB — Investing','{"skill-progression","financial"}','{"phase","financial","foundations","weeks","investment","strategy","works","broken","foundation","sequence","matters","emergency","fund","debt","elimination"}','[0.01326832,-0.07377079,0.02082117,-0.00680237,-0.05045458,0.03702018,0.01198474,-0.04483865,-0.0130394,-0.08657535,-0.00490935,-0.08997726,-0.03322319,0.02216927,0.01197717,0.02890961,0.05561391,0.02366944,0.11915644,-0.06638823,-0.08063523,-0.02268159,0.02217425,0.03113827,-0.11221851,0.04840659,-0.15188819,0.00177408,-0.07089109,-0.16194999,0.00120626,0.10472997,-0.05769889,0.05586246,-0.00086723,-0.06472918,0.0167125,0.04725479,0.04472889,0.01812513,-0.0361826,0.09715256,-0.03083976,0.08503012,-0.04286178,0.0262088,0.14354557,0.00412364,0.03825276,-0.03600081,0.03273157,0.05965758,-0.0726186,-0.01545554,-0.04320172,-0.01823682,0.02197221,-0.02670359,-0.03542911,-0.00244059,0.07815638,0.01160558,0.0210226,0.04762093,-0.07519374,-0.07025574,-0.04811057,0.00428596,-0.0154477,0.04312136,0.09128892,-0.03780784,0.02967064,0.01128683,0.03171537,0.04298917,0.05077834,-0.01405076,0.01141706,0.00738426,-0.00831486,-0.01793632,0.01323054,0.05508509,0.02571132,-0.00052345,0.00767187,0.04151464,-0.00862757,-0.02927362,-0.04826701,0.02169448,0.01892933,-0.05925181,0.0279113,-0.05463842,0.04695624,0.01677481,0.03828775,0.02159428,0.02205978,-0.00048781,0.02922768,-0.0700995,0.10679959,0.00914589,0.05255216,-0.07577916,0.02387115,-0.05488551,0.05290651,0.05993051,0.00789159,-0.05397403,-0.03570036,0.01399587,0.00164395,0.00610129,-0.06274292,0.05771701,0.01836013,-0.04812998,0.06800827,-0.00635753,0.04850036,0.00928409,-0.06370509,0.02407139,0.01965574,0.04399038,0.007205,0.03895297,-0.024133,0.07618673,0.02013559,0.05545833,-0.00688955,-0.01402908,0.00489068,0.03134967,-0.00537808,-0.02517594,0.1020122,0.0194034,-0.04588284,-0.01824093,-0.07780