INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('4d2e5194-e704-4046-921b-de9cdb540134','md-mental-health-phase-1-baseline-and-fundamental-practices-weeks-1','Phase 1: Baseline and Fundamental Practices (Weeks 1–4)

Mental health is not the absence of symptoms — it is a set of daily practices that build resilience, emotional regulation, and cognitive flexibility. These practices have the strongest evidence base across clinical literature.

The evidence hierarchy for mental health interventions:
1. Exercise (strongest evidence — equivalent to antidepressants for mild-moderate depression)
2. Sleep (bidirectional: poor sleep causes mental health issues; mental health issues cause poor sleep)
3. Social connection (loneliness is as harmful to health as smoking 15 cigarettes per day — Holt-Lunstad)
4. Sunlight exposure (20-30 min daily reduces depression risk by 35%)
5. Journaling and expressive writing (Pennebaker research: 20 min of expressive writing 3x = therapeutic effect)

Week 1–2: Physical foundation
- Exercise: 20-30 min moderate intensity, 3-5 days per week
- This is not optional — BDNF (brain-derived neurotrophic factor) from exercise is the closest thing to a natural antidepressant
- If motivation is low: commit to 5 min walking. Walking 5 min/day is categorically better than 0 min.

Week 3–4: Social and environmental practices
- One meaningful social interaction per day (in-person is stronger than digital, but digital counts)
- Sunlight within 30 min of waking, minimum 10 min outside daily
- Begin 5-minute daily reflection (what happened today? how did it feel? what would I do differently?)

Milestone: Exercise 3×/week maintained for 4 consecutive weeks. Daily reflection practiced 5 of 7 days.','Coheren Domain KB — Mental Health','{"skill-progression","health"}','{"phase","baseline","fundamental","practices","weeks","mental","health","absence","symptoms","daily","build","resilience","emotional","regulation","cognitive"}','[0.04218375,0.04312023,0.01290713,-0.03369685,-0.05213407,-0.12380926,-0.03927376,0.01038386,-0.04905355,-0.10199033,-0.03659093,-0.03301019,0.01865818,-0.01847761,0.12787288,-0.03013415,-0.00525742,0.00563579,0.10648018,0.01957125,-0.07397453,-0.05276423,-0.02842947,0.03258216,-0.07509277,0.03924905,-0.04868813,-0.07572084,-0.20727332,-0.08110659,0.07943796,-0.09712613,-0.015522,0.03602764,0.08444406,0.11428054,0.01323888,0.07012734,0.05574346,0.02760203,-0.01464606,0.03300941,0.00928764,0.10134438,-0.01732824,0.01562509,0.02656473,-0.05736311,0.01141464,-0.07127375,0.00705941,0.12164024,-0.01101057,0.06852879,-0.04727205,-0.00655382,0.04663335,-0.00437413,-0.02543582,-0.06522927,-0.01696524,0.06394358,-0.02096831,0.0382193,0.02825413,-0.00112138,-0.04386624,-0.03224865,-0.00684152,0.00556671,0.05157388,-0.02777248,0.03570613,0.02665806,0.02250027,0.01157436,0.03204405,-0.02813992,-0.02982527,0.04322074,-0.02319687,-0.00793823,0.05367859,0.03932492,0.01245626,0.00876316,-0.08695853,0.05081766,-0.02133649,-0.00215976,-0.0767156,-0.07213663,-0.06586464,-0.04330198,0.03426817,-0.0218097,0.01883917,0.04082412,-0.00598252,-0.01625236,0.04569108,0.05485364,0.05105433,0.0093455,0.00351212,0.0634507,0.03206095,0.0158164,0.01539531,-0.02552417,0.04830441,0.03153462,-0.00203363,-0.03086414,0.02077538,-0.01927827,0.05560705,-0.02188094,-0.05189828,-0.0086576,-0.01719572,-0.06345596,-0.00150212,0.03542507,0.06339522,0.01611099,-0.01222722,-0.03803176,-0.01749504,0.06486641,-0.01914938,0.01372459,-0.00056961,0.03691557,0.00926509,0.06193552,-0.01728494,0.02138667,0.02835346,0.01757233,0.00371731,-0.01585935,0.00183237,0.04371962,-0.03502465,-0.034