INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('368bd5d7-b51e-4ce4-af4c-eab5e2abb929','md-mental-health-phase-2-emotional-regulation-skills-weeks-5-10','Phase 2: Emotional Regulation Skills (Weeks 5–10)

Emotional regulation is a learnable skill, not a fixed trait. The goal is not to eliminate negative emotions but to increase response flexibility — being able to choose how to respond rather than reacting automatically.

Mindfulness basics (secular, evidence-based):
- Attention training: notice where your attention is, redirect it intentionally
- Start: 5 min daily of focused breathing (Headspace, Waking Up, or self-guided)
- After 2 weeks: extend to 10 min
- Evidence: 8 weeks of 10 min/day mindfulness practice measurably changes amygdala reactivity

Cognitive reappraisal (from CBT):
- Identify automatic thoughts: when upset, write the thought down immediately ("I''''m terrible at this")
- Challenge: Is this thought a fact or an interpretation? What evidence exists for and against?
- Reframe: "I''''m struggling with this specific thing right now" vs "I''''m terrible at this"
- Practice: write 1 thought + challenge per day for 21 days

The feelings wheel:
- Most people have a limited emotional vocabulary (happy, sad, angry, fine)
- Identifying emotions with precision ("I''''m frustrated because I feel invisible in this meeting") reduces their intensity and creates response options
- Use a feelings wheel (downloadable free) to expand vocabulary

Journaling protocols that work:
- Gratitude: 3 specific things (not "family" — "my daughter''''s laugh when I tickle her today")
- Expressive writing: 20 min of uncensored writing about a stressor (Pennebaker protocol, 3x/week)
- Values journaling: "Did I act in alignment with my values today? Where did I fall short?"

Milestone: Mindfulness practice at 10 min/day for 21 consecutive days. One automatic thought challenged and reframed per day for 14 days.','Coheren Domain KB — Mental Health','{"skill-progression","health"}','{"phase","emotional","regulation","skills","weeks","learnable","skill","fixed","trait","goal","eliminate","negative","emotions","increase","response"}','[0.12125271,0.04874949,0.04409193,-0.03656553,0.03861419,-0.11924703,-0.00042916,0.09123087,0.01934857,-0.1539931,-0.05753541,-0.02343163,-0.04782869,0.01001197,0.14875881,-0.00714808,0.06584508,-0.00523367,0.08954691,-0.03843328,-0.10515437,-0.00966191,-0.09143595,0.05417183,-0.05863615,-0.0059991,0.02677645,-0.0706264,-0.0812864,-0.03719403,0.06068622,-0.05750793,-0.0715877,-0.02314595,0.03246662,0.07891252,0.01312141,0.06288461,0.00067901,0.06353629,0.01375725,-0.01715167,0.06204404,0.03933997,-0.04296404,-0.01700378,0.06808475,-0.05244744,-0.0115355,0.01074853,0.06483672,0.06935472,-0.05509342,0.02235372,-0.05319391,0.07887297,0.03783099,0.02148976,-0.00234663,-0.02472311,-0.02882017,0.1253932,-0.01782168,0.02590558,-0.05637066,0.00945557,-0.0250899,-0.01647405,-0.04432766,-0.02204771,0.08638605,0.05476784,0.05738781,0.00663353,0.06124569,-0.01742953,0.02345734,0.01584046,-0.01352153,-0.03237282,0.04798369,-0.01335235,0.05623558,0.0339226,0.06877746,0.02217838,-0.09970585,0.03258778,-0.00527024,-0.08029194,-0.05863531,0.00966979,-0.0854878,-0.00650131,-0.01640116,0.00308855,0.05900245,0.00452069,-0.04660974,0.01085417,0.01292589,0.05925842,-0.00233918,0.03643793,0.05435843,0.04888839,0.0320981,-0.03191306,0.05105446,0.00805466,-0.00162161,0.11747602,0.02940132,-0.02387345,-0.04422972,-0.00262012,0.05940374,0.04944875,-0.01708799,0.03268679,0.01535811,-0.01099108,0.02883562,0.02780354,-0.04150914,-0.01650563,0.01898435,0.02169896,-0.02818886,0.08878717,-0.010838,0.01148158,0.00704761,0.08692877,-0.00716423,0.04617454,-0.05184881,0.04311597,0.07566988,0.02644328,-0.00023737,0.01732181,0.00873886,0.08918019,-0