INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('fb7d6355-41e3-4d66-85a1-8eac41a1a98b','md-mental-health-phase-3-resilience-building-and-sustainable-mainte','Phase 3: Resilience Building and Sustainable Maintenance (Weeks 11–24)

Resilience is not never struggling — it is the ability to recover from struggle faster. These practices build the capacity for recovery.

Stress inoculation:
- Controlled voluntary exposure to mild stress builds tolerance: cold showers, hard exercise, fasting for 16 hours
- Deliberate discomfort teaches the nervous system that distress is survivable and temporary
- Breath work for nervous system regulation: box breathing (4-4-4-4) activates parasympathetic state within 90 seconds

Professional support:
- Therapy is not only for crisis — it is maintenance care, like the gym for the mind
- Types: CBT (best evidence for anxiety, depression), DBT (emotional regulation), ACT (values-based behavior)
- If therapy is financially inaccessible: Workbook-based CBT (Feeling Good by David Burns) has strong evidence for self-directed use

Building a support network:
- Identify 3-5 people you can contact when struggling — these must be explicitly maintained relationships
- One relationship that requires vulnerability per week (share something real, not surface-level)
- Community engagement: belonging to something larger than yourself consistently predicts wellbeing

Review and adjust (quarterly):
- Assess: sleep, exercise, social connection, stress levels — these are the metrics
- What''s working? What''s missing? What''s becoming automatic vs. requiring effort?

Milestone: One social relationship explicitly invested in per week. One professional support contact made (therapist, coach, or support group).','Coheren Domain KB — Mental Health','{"skill-progression","health"}','{"phase","resilience","building","sustainable","maintenance","weeks","never","struggling","ability","recover","struggle","faster","practices","build","capacity"}','[0.11980833,0.04881063,-0.01451414,-0.02916454,-0.02055274,-0.08655629,-0.06032207,0.1017685,-0.0549227,-0.10752708,0.03898598,-0.09298139,-0.01036497,0.01494804,0.15842365,0.00500703,-0.01971357,0.02179887,0.08692529,-0.01974962,-0.07303702,-0.10320726,-0.08501519,0.05725108,-0.08563609,0.04989438,-0.07402802,0.01354011,-0.19575745,-0.09493734,0.11772286,0.04081215,-0.06096604,0.01313626,0.12334903,0.03600924,0.0316525,-0.00443539,-0.00535399,0.05752658,-0.02340575,0.00735395,-0.05245419,0.101491,-0.02097028,-0.06461233,0.02854393,-0.08683818,0.02907868,-0.04262023,0.01760919,0.08821982,-0.06889369,0.03424437,-0.06507824,-0.00083719,0.02399621,-0.00219434,-0.00968436,0.01075065,-0.05839576,0.03950421,-0.03262429,0.08865459,-0.02098893,-0.00951872,0.01497578,-0.07586043,-0.02017044,0.01388235,0.07438558,0.05566562,-0.0179956,0.10038815,0.05025414,-0.00824008,0.03557599,-0.02227334,-0.01747593,-0.03073684,-0.0066764,0.05516786,0.06044687,0.00525188,-0.00502497,0.0075124,-0.06632686,-0.02571746,0.03551726,-0.00902544,-0.0331463,0.00899535,-0.03902208,0.01501145,0.01611349,-0.05961541,0.00122273,-0.06184999,-0.01644661,0.00614683,0.06816663,0.04438766,-0.01856073,-0.03059285,0.00137731,-0.01264406,0.07731372,-0.04096171,-0.00494165,0.02520454,-0.00272843,0.08133461,0.01784258,-0.03339624,0.00951846,0.01840866,0.06394461,-0.00763833,0.0125309,0.01602047,0.04118863,0.00888599,-0.01433732,0.03063713,0.04110875,0.04468075,0.01994051,0.00600985,-0.02205324,0.04470892,-0.01833763,0.02483995,-0.01989277,0.03178168,-0.01276682,0.01877852,0.00124113,-0.00067088,0.04993413,-0.00167496,0.01092169,-0.0197034,