INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('be9ef046-0f40-4f18-bf1c-198edb919d12','md-sleep-phase-3-advanced-optimization-weeks-7-12','Phase 3: Advanced Optimization (Weeks 7–12)

Once the foundations are working, targeted interventions can further improve deep sleep and REM.

Caffeine timing:
- Adenosine (sleep pressure) accumulates throughout the day and is cleared during sleep
- Caffeine blocks adenosine receptors — it doesn''t reduce sleepiness, it masks it
- Caffeine half-life: 5-7 hours. Quarter-life: 10-14 hours.
- Last caffeine by 1 PM for most people (adjust: if bedtime is 11 PM, stop caffeine by 1-2 PM)

Alcohol:
- Alcohol is a sedative, not a sleep aid — it sedates, which is not the same as sleep
- Even 2 drinks reduces slow-wave sleep by 20% and REM by 30%
- If drinking: minimum 4 hours between last drink and sleep

Exercise timing:
- Exercise improves sleep quality — even 20 min of moderate exercise per day
- Vigorous exercise within 2 hours of bed elevates cortisol — avoid or move to earlier
- Morning exercise: strongest positive effect on evening sleep quality

Supplements (evidence-ranked):
- Magnesium glycinate (300-400mg): small but real effect on sleep quality. Well-tolerated. Evidence: moderate.
- Melatonin (0.3-1mg, NOT the typical 5-10mg): helps with circadian phase shifting (jet lag, shift work). Does not improve sleep quality at high doses — lower doses are more effective.
- Chamomile, valerian: mild anxiolytic effects. Evidence: weak but real.
- Avoid: alcohol, antihistamines (Benadryl), cannabis — all suppress REM

Milestone: Average sleep quality ≥7/10 for 2 consecutive weeks. Consistent wake time maintained 6 of 7 days.','Coheren Domain KB — Sleep Optimization','{"skill-progression","health"}','{"phase","advanced","optimization","weeks","once","foundations","working","targeted","interventions","further","improve","deep","sleep","caffeine","timing"}','[0.01889039,0.07717225,-0.05140586,-0.03015058,0.03572535,-0.01112733,-0.03782255,0.05896887,0.02995129,-0.16658512,0.00559117,-0.04282245,-0.10201065,-0.09274072,0.01978175,-0.08651806,-0.01910628,-0.06859542,0.02986767,-0.0319005,-0.04593372,-0.06054808,-0.0802019,0.1557125,-0.0658463,0.05237183,-0.01416616,-0.06728798,-0.05216111,0.01025814,-0.00411466,-0.0953715,-0.02174639,0.02433312,0.05937226,0.00234234,0.07063619,0.0413384,0.04394661,-0.01318781,-0.05416575,0.02715266,-0.0142344,0.02451653,0.07308748,0.02931417,-0.00055472,0.00972697,0.03632136,-0.04505801,-0.09428561,0.09650502,-0.03579333,0.09743455,-0.05272652,0.07915206,0.08850672,-0.0441711,0.01966888,-0.06450506,-0.01610584,0.00139694,0.02766549,-0.0398938,0.00159747,0.00899499,0.060429,-0.03317956,0.03662408,-0.04740535,0.076587,0.05374343,-0.02058918,0.03376742,-0.03813215,-0.01479957,-0.02388419,-0.00406215,0.01130995,0.02651568,-0.08619387,0.07503945,-0.00682378,0.074263,-0.03293389,-0.03092411,-0.09710713,0.01521422,0.04701078,-0.02791893,-0.03808104,-0.02728322,-0.01588295,-0.06660795,0.07571217,-0.02225552,0.13957435,-0.02396386,-0.03863489,0.006088,-0.06418376,-0.02938528,0.01500531,0.05214237,0.04161349,0.05087679,-0.06224039,-0.02879218,-0.00348223,-0.01179225,0.0501221,0.04716878,0.00689468,-0.02929916,0.04995376,0.01514408,0.04198943,-0.01634718,0.01559582,0.02677035,0.03464074,0.03792313,-0.02954575,0.01711452,0.04447716,0.05525038,-0.02484031,-0.04673941,-0.0327194,0.0245954,-0.02431144,0.02628089,0.04294462,0.00336214,-0.02147737,0.04954221,-0.06627867,-0.04331702,-0.0002505,0.05299998,0.01896027,0.02585289,-0.01046391,0.06767068,-0.01724621,-0.02529