INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('52f534d6-8dd6-42d9-8210-9ea52c944e78','md-morning-routine-phase-1-anchor-and-wake-time-weeks-1-2','Phase 1: Anchor and Wake Time (Weeks 1–2)

A morning routine begins with a fixed wake time. Everything else is built on that anchor. Without a consistent wake time, the routine shifts daily and never becomes automatic.

Wake time selection:
- Choose a wake time you can maintain 7 days/week (including weekends)
- 5 AM only works if you''re asleep by 9:30 PM. Be honest about bedtime.
- Even a 6:30 AM wake time with a quality routine beats a chaotic 5 AM routine
- Formula: target wake time = target bedtime - 7.5 hours (5 complete sleep cycles)

The first 10 minutes are the highest leverage:
- Phone must not be touched in the first 10 minutes (notifications activate reactivity mode immediately)
- Put the phone in a different room or use an analog alarm clock
- First action should be physical: stand up, drink water, open curtains

Week 1: Single anchor habit
- Pick ONE morning action and make it non-negotiable
- Not 5 things. One thing. This is the anchor for everything that follows.
- Best single anchor: making your bed (immediately visible evidence of accomplishment) + drinking 500ml water
- Milestone: 14 consecutive days of the same single anchor action within 10 min of waking

Week 2: Extend to 20-minute block
- Anchor (5 min) + one addition (15 min): choose from options below based on your primary goal
- Option A: 15 min journaling or reflection
- Option B: 10 min movement + 5 min planning
- Option C: 15 min focused reading (not news or social)
- Milestone: 14 consecutive days of 20-minute morning block completed before any screen time','Coheren Domain KB — Morning Routine','{"skill-progression","lifestyle"}','{"phase","anchor","wake","time","weeks","morning","routine","begins","fixed","everything","else","built","without","consistent","shifts"}','[0.00592822,0.03426309,0.04553213,-0.0390515,0.00496234,-0.05623256,-0.11884308,0.08110236,0.05821788,-0.18483965,-0.13484779,-0.00130299,-0.08011007,0.07251965,0.00246993,-0.00025195,0.02338035,-0.03578348,0.0755,0.00999412,-0.11458683,-0.09694851,-0.09124251,0.13015753,-0.03569995,0.01583532,0.02877447,-0.03832905,-0.09157388,-0.03925907,0.02881075,-0.03728136,-0.02807279,0.03759877,0.02181547,-0.00830827,0.08336491,0.16245627,0.08808205,0.04097706,0.02049417,-0.00707808,-0.06920382,0.06450708,0.01928095,0.00722247,0.04620811,0.02770566,0.1161807,-0.04766995,-0.02871564,0.08791407,0.03217234,-0.01384463,-0.05729585,0.01077634,0.08047903,-0.03740045,-0.00090178,-0.01781146,-0.0284046,0.07538262,-0.02767265,-0.00946425,-0.07160606,-0.07254639,0.001176,-0.00255078,-0.04800503,0.00630983,0.04085183,-0.00012405,0.02421055,0.03881009,0.0070857,0.02849345,-0.02942415,-0.0517809,0.02570229,0.05495297,-0.02948848,0.03050411,0.03144559,0.05777164,0.02607213,-0.00798961,-0.09753384,0.03264346,0.02589363,0.03275662,-0.06058478,0.0022252,-0.03543412,-0.09361993,0.04713166,0.05809312,0.06323522,-0.05480087,-0.0247177,0.00585853,0.02017731,0.00305015,0.01782792,0.01703848,0.01852619,-0.0075301,0.06008904,-0.05313266,-0.03709117,-0.01012104,0.02529933,0.04466017,-0.00345567,-0.03934717,-0.03074126,0.02491744,-0.01736691,-0.00921029,0.03382013,0.02368073,-0.01852739,-0.02255785,0.00693587,0.0265483,0.01982769,-0.01763867,-0.01886728,-0.00919729,-0.00140395,0.02185536,-0.04144903,0.05525097,0.01234124,0.05551534,0.00683707,0.04725706,-0.03056245,-0.03758188,-0.00749282,0.0787512,0.04606677,-0.01533449,0.01189891,0.00361769,-0.01118985,0.00276787,-0.0092121,0.02645644,0.02718711,