7,0.02192472,-0.01300173,-0.04129339,-0.004817,-0.00664726,0.01858446,-0.0146376,-0.00107189,-0.05278926,0.00238805,-0.01052309,0.01377365,0.00248878,0.00021778,-0.01216626,-0.02642866,0.00513047,-0.00503038,0.01594938,0.00956886,0.0009348,0.030964,0.00878154,-0.00146034,-0.01630238,-0.00074437,-0.00582971,0.00079166,0.02828852,-0.01465855,-0.00113497,0.0192634,-0.01769153,0.00783954,-0.01815351,0.00688212,-0.0034564,-0.00595413,0.01886309,-0.02131386,0.02968663,-0.01094404,-0.0137656,-0.00750672,0.03509253,-0.01581768,-0.01377181,0.00348893,-0.00332108,-0.03031322,-0.01257923,0.01439051,-0.03394538,0.03795512,-0.02591718,-0.00666778,0.0295385,0.01600418,0.01029827,-0.03394376,-0.00632251,-0.01721001,-0.00940147,0.03854898,-0.01291024,0.02035975,0.01040149,-0.00233863]'::vector,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,'{}','raptor_summary',1,'{"low-motivation"}','2026-04-02T05:57:24.52708+00:00') ON CONFLICT (chunk_id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('528ff022-8e30-4e5f-bb80-ba0a166b3d7b','raptor_l1_Psychology_Research_c1','The core insight shared across various studies is that self-compassion plays a crucial role in habit change, particularly in maintaining motivation and adherence. This concept is rooted in the theory of self-compassion, which was extensively researched by Kristin Neff. Key findings suggest that treating oneself with kindness, understanding, and acceptance, rather than self-criticism, leads to more effective habit formation and adherence. When individuals practice self-compassion, they are more likely to approach challenges with a growth mindset, acknowledging difficulties without judgment, and are less likely to give up. This approach can be particularly beneficial in habit coaching, as it encourages individuals to develop a more supportive and non-judgmental relationship with themselves, ultimately leading to greater success in achieving their goals.','Psychology Research (summary)','{"struggling","mindset"}','{"compassion","kind","forgive","guilt","shame","fail"}','[-0.03612313,0.03413516,0.00573496,-0.11759442,-0.00212676,-0.06123647,0.03725111,0.13363963,0.06022644,-0.04115754,0.0080349,-0.03188571,-0.01624773,0.06782366,0.07283181,0.1378332,0.00955975,0.01458871,0.07252079,-0.0056075,-0.03227073,-0.04366536,0.03243519,0.05534982,-0.01330405,-0.12425461,0.06358219,-0.10746913,-0.06927358,-0.11584336,0.004951,-0.01297094,-0.05081742,0.02866109,0.02788039,0.04645457,-0.02040195,-0.02357772,0.04602415,-0.00204088,0.01480172,-0.01445524,-0.10143164,-0.02653025,0.04029461,0.01557912,0.00370779,-0.05145855,0.08028775,-0.03880373,0.06290487,0.07561623,0.03635572,0.03463997,-0.07100948,0.01656489,0.0612475,-0.02513883,0.03531853,-0