,-0.00541418,0.04899061,0.02134125,0.02609739,0.00372721,-0.00059953,-0.02242839,-0.00351658,0.00167994,0.01500065,-0.01371447,-0.03293635,-0.01159724,-0.02239534,0.01573611,0.00775034,0.00802804,-0.02318668,-0.00106324,-0.01436745,0.04427143,-0.0166645,-0.00367999,-0.03276744,0.023494,-0.01266522,0.0046884,-0.01504637,-0.00787476,-0.00102764,-0.01840032,0.02250472,-0.02002091,0.02983384,0.00849594,0.00076316,0.04338509,0.01610009,-0.00326301,0.019933,-0.00866268,0.0159727,0.01902018,0.00240403,0.00339985,0.00938409,0.01662658,-0.00405536,0.01986359,-0.00042361,-0.01288745,-0.00410054,-0.00033477,0.01911549,-0.00286127,0.04310545,0.00522265,-0.01174392,-0.01985133,-0.00115951,-0.04037107,-0.01897213,-0.0211477,-0.02359017,-0.00164867,0.0020209,0.01881539,-0.01639806,0.02746792,-0.01575549,0.04323624,-0.00368524,0.00299958,-0.00553751,-0.0353561,-0.00709657,0.03088511,-0.02296258,0.04413751,0.03665328,0.00013322,-0.02149479,0.03146369]'::vector,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,'{}','raptor_summary',1,'{"md-skill-development-phase-1-skill-gap-analysis-and-learning-plan-weeks","md-skill-development-phase-2-skill-acquisition-through-projects-weeks-3","md-skill-development-phase-3-application-and-feedback-loops-weeks-13-20","md-skill-development-deliberate-practice-principles-applied-to-careers","md-skill-development-common-pitfalls"}','2026-04-02T06:05:57.776568+00:00') ON CONFLICT (chunk_id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('88d04bb5-5d54-4800-b144-b3a587c83b51','raptor_l1_Coheren_Coaching_KB___Perfectionism_c1','The core insight shared across these passages is that perfectionism is not about having high standards, but rather about the belief that performance determines worth. This leads to a range of maladaptive behaviors, including procrastination, endless revision loops, and selective avoidance. The key theory referenced is the concept of "identity reframe," which suggests that individuals can shift their identity from a perfectionist to a functional one by accumulating behavioral evidence of imperfect but completed work. The most actionable finding for habit coaching is the importance of setting a "good enough" standard, which involves defining a minimum viable acceptable quality and producing to that standard first, rather than striving for perfection. This can be achieved through techniques such as time-boxing, deliberate imperfection exercises, and the "ship it" gate. By adopting these strategies, individuals can build tolerance for imperfection and develop a more functional and productive approach to work and creativity.','Coheren Coaching KB — Perfectionism (summary)','{"coaching","behavior-change"}','{"identity","reframe","perfectionist''s","high","standards","only","show","work","proud","functional","ship","regularly","improve","through","feedback","understanding","perfectionism","belief","performance","determines","worth","high-standards","people","produce","excellent","perfectionists","avoid","good","enough","standard","psychological","lowering","defining","what","success","actually","requires","protocol","define","minimum","viable","time-boxing","treatment","time","constraints","externalize","judgment","tim