907,-0.00410392,-0.01501536,0.00638706,-0.01386329,-0.00495499,-0.03358319,0.01449961,-0.01587229,0.03737853,-0.01463239,0.01546734,0.00943219,-0.0184916,-0.03863452,-0.0292414,0.03455178,0.00254208,0.00923374,0.04410391,-0.00555955,-0.01293433,-0.02001836,-0.03491236,0.05929163,0.00648028,0.00045932,-0.00168768,-0.00535505,0.01633101,0.01244218,0.03275976,-0.03989866,-0.00399633,0.00143111,-0.00770977,0.00208901,-0.00405404,0.0593997,-0.00399923,-0.00247961,-0.03691951,0.03262483,-0.03988492,-0.00529491,0.00464706,-0.00111006,0.00144342,-0.03308541,0.02483043,-0.05069268,0.01824904,-0.01468002,0.00109338,0.02245698,0.02632555,0.00566195,-0.0031427,0.00315243,0.0111859,0.00580159,0.04385085,0.02021341,0.00219274,0.03388722,0.03125297]'::vector,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,'{}','raptor_summary',1,'{"md-running-phase-3-5k-to-10k-weeks-9-16","md-running-phase-1-foundation-run-walk-to-continuous-running-","md-running-phase-2-building-continuous-running-weeks-5-8","md-running-injury-prevention-protocol","md-running-common-pitfalls"}','2026-04-02T06:08:24.521796+00:00') ON CONFLICT (chunk_id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('df5cda79-3183-4cc0-98a2-2ff43dc199a4','raptor_l1_Coheren_Domain_KB___Music_c1','The core insight shared across these passages is that effective learning and mastery of a musical instrument require a deliberate and structured approach, focusing on slow and correct repetition, rather than fast and sloppy practice. This is rooted in the concept of motor memory, which is built through the cerebellum and basal ganglia. The key theory and framework referenced is the idea of gradual skill acquisition, where each phase of learning builds upon the previous one, with a focus on technique, music theory, and performance.

The most actionable finding for habit coaching is the importance of setting milestones and tracking progress, such as playing a song from start to finish at slow tempo, or playing 5 complete songs from memory at full tempo with correct rhythm. Additionally, the use of a metronome and recording oneself are essential tools for developing good time feel and accurate self-assessment. By incorporating these strategies into practice, individuals can avoid common pitfalls such as practicing too fast or ignoring technique, and make steady progress towards musical mastery.','Coheren Domain KB — Music (summary)','{"skill-progression","creative"}','{"phase","foundational","technique","weeks","music","skill","stored","motor","memory","cerebellum","basal","ganglia","built","through","slow","expanding","repertoire","theory","songs","become","vehicle","learn","context","care","about","practice","performance","musicality","technical","competence","musical","expression","different","develops","feel","timing","ability","make","common","pitfalls","practicing","fast","encoding","wrong","patterns","thing","unlearn","later","skipping","metronome","good","time"}','[0.05891411,0.01820246,0.03821796,-0.01709465,0.04766523,-0.03214622,-0.07246909,0.07998589,-0.00534916,-0.08843895,-0.05583502,-0.05063447,-0.00597806,0.09375401,0.0802574,0.04071262,0.00552327,-0.02007581,0.01371082,0.01576948,-0.10149153,0.12222307,-0.02667807,0.04163064,0.02714056,-0.13838275,0.00436131,-0.15943307,-0.05546468,-0.04929566,-0.06135258,0.06929044,-0.0688381,0.08070083,-0.01049702,-0.05192496,0.01252179,-0.00334553,0.00749486,0.05374648,0.05113521,0.03293611,-0.12680933,-0.01220064,0.058998,0.0041649,0.07067794,-0.02231099,0.01206367,-0.10576988,0.04248025,0.11309761,0.01267952,-0.02702169,-0.04114716,0.04714538,0.074295,-0.04990999,0.00250289,-0.03365779,0.03015834,-0.03147541,-0.05312563,0.04371319,-0.07697936,-0.04667954,-0.00216245,-0.0031187,-0.03826668,-0.01684551,0.10326751,0.03124149,0.00095814,-0.03658