,-0.02821312,-0.008983,0.00272701,-0.01297037,0.02318971,-0.04064365,0.00558589,-0.00625969,0.01259814,0.00080864,-0.00028201,-0.01154375,-0.02194515,-0.0065739,0.04545496,-0.02013121,0.06093675,0.03630036,0.01510134,-0.00913824,0.03032441]'::vector,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,'{}','raptor_summary',2,'{"raptor_l1_dreyfus_skill_acquisition_c1","raptor_l1_ericsson_deliberate_practice_c1","raptor_l1_ericsson_deliberate_practice_c2","raptor_l1_lally_habit_automaticity_c1"}','2026-04-02T06:11:42.34891+00:00') ON CONFLICT (chunk_id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('a638b21c-35fd-4b28-bb5f-9dc3389283ec','raptor_l2_habit_formation_c5','A unifying theme across these summaries is the importance of strategic planning and cue-based interventions in habit formation and maintenance. Research-backed insights highlight the significance of context consistency, habit duration, and cue specificity in promoting resilient habits. Key findings include: 

1. Habits require at least 66 days to become automatic, and significant complexity should not be added to the foundation phase before day 30, suggesting the need for coaches to design curricula with explicit disruption recovery protocols.
2. Implementation intentions, which involve specifying when, where, and how to perform a task, significantly enhance follow-through and habit formation, particularly when the triggering cue is specific, observable, personally relevant, and temporally precise.
3. Changing habits requires a deep understanding of the dynamic interplay between cues, routines, and rewards, and can be achieved by keeping the same cue and reward, and replacing only the routine.

These insights connect to habit formation and behavior change coaching by emphasizing the importance of strategic planning, cue-based interventions, and gradual habit development. A key takeaway for coaches is that by incorporating these evidence-based strategies into their practices, they can empower individuals to overcome motivational barriers and establish consistent, resilient habits.','habit-formation knowledge (document summary)','{"habit-formation","behavior-change"}','{"habit","fragility","phase","transitions","even","fully","automatic","habits","disrupted","context","change","moving","travel","illness","relationship","application","curriculum","timeline","design","never","promise","automaticity","before","research","average","days","foundation","reach","core","framework","peter","gollwitzer''s","implementation","intentions","addresses","most","frustrating","gaps","behavior","intention-action","people","structure","intention","format","situation","occurs","response","differs","simple","goal","intend","exercise","week","specifying","exactly","works","three","mechanisms","strategic","if-then","link","creates","mental","association","between","situational","intended","action","encountered","quantified","effect","sizes","meta-analysis","studies","gollwitzer","sheeran","2006","overall","medium-large","comparable","points","test","performance","trivial","matters","much","orbell","hodgkins","1997","showed","triggering","must","specific","observable","feel","tired","coping","planning","sniehotta","extension","2005","schwarzer","scholz","adds","second","layer","obstacle-specific","plans","anticipated","barriers","task","task-level","every","assigned","anchor","environmental","user''s","routine","intake","evidence","summary","coaching","having","plan","doubles","triples","follow-through","vague","loop","follows","stages","reward","trigger","initiates","location","time","emotional","state","keystone","certain","create","ripple","effects","transform","other","areas","l