.01255067,-0.01371025,0.00412383,0.01091081,-0.02972225,-0.00781316,-0.02512958,0.01902165,-0.02468907,-0.01382007,0.01537975,-0.01190919,-0.00961063,0.02335585,-0.01968034,-0.00964433,0.01785941,-0.02324395,0.00594572,0.03097322,-0.00255536,-0.03746687,-0.03967921,0.03977561,-0.05225886,0.04670847,-0.01899221,0.00854619,-0.00037474,0.01850233,0.02701978,0.01793275,-0.01914456,0.01919496,-0.02980407,0.05043313,-0.0021583,0.01473273,0.03133936,0.00495137]'::vector,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{}',NULL,NULL,'{}','raptor_summary',2,'{"raptor_l1_Coheren_Domain_KB___Morning_Routine_c1"}','2026-04-02T06:14:34.288307+00:00') ON CONFLICT (chunk_id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, chunk_id, content, source, categories, keywords, embedding, enriched_content, framework, content_type, applicable_stones, coaching_stage, evidence_level, emotion_context, chunk_type, raptor_level, raptor_source_ids, created_at) VALUES ('6a3373f0-a9d0-4c0c-be6e-4d3c2a7f8619','raptor_l2_coaching_c1','The unifying theme across these summaries is the importance of designing and implementing strategies that foster confidence, competence, and consistency in individuals, ultimately driving behavior change and habit formation. Research-backed insights that stand out include: 

1. The significance of early wins and small, achievable successes in building competence and confidence through mastery experiences and vicarious experiences, as per Bandura''s theory of self-efficacy.
2. The value of connecting new skills to existing knowledge, making incremental learning explicit, and using phrases that emphasize the logical structure of tasks to build confidence and extend existing skills.
3. The importance of reducing session startup friction and implementing a recovery protocol when a break occurs, as per the "Never Miss Twice" Rule, to build resilience and maintain consistency in habits.

These insights connect to habit formation and behavior change coaching by highlighting the need to create a supportive environment that acknowledges setbacks, celebrates small wins, and fosters a sense of identity and self-discipline. By implementing these strategies, coaches can empower individuals to build confidence, competence, and consistency, ultimately driving lasting behavior change. 

Key takeaway: By focusing on small, achievable successes, connecting new skills to existing knowledge, and implementing recovery protocols, coaches can help individuals build confidence, competence, and consistency, ultimately driving lasting behavior change.','coaching knowledge (document summary)','{"coaching","motivation","habit-formation"}','{"past","performance","confidence","foundation","often","ignores","evidence","brain''s","negativity","bias","makes","failure","memories","more","available","skill","inventory","low-confidence","people","accurate","picture","what","can''t","inaccurate","exercise","list","everything","already","know","calibration","over","perfection","success","criteria","users","calibrated","current","ability","ideal","complete","pull-ups","better","understanding","domain-specific","global","trait","someone","highly","confident","work","socially","means","built","through","competence","development","guaranteed","early","wins","first","weeks","goal","must","produce","feel","real","person","design","challenge","level","evidence-based","self-efficacy","building","bandura''s","four","sources","specific","domain","mastery","experiences","strongest","experiencing","progressively","connections","every","skills","acquired","making","explicit","builds","protocol","curriculum","inconsistency","pattern","strong","start","momentum","skip","guilt","extended","break","restart","overambitious","plan","repeat","never","miss","twice","rule","james","clear","missing","once","accident","habit","eliminates","binary","maintain","streak","sprint-based","structure","three-day","micro-sprints","reduce","psychological","weight","long","commitments","sprint","days","active","practice","scaled","availability","environmental","triggers","consistency","easier","behavior","triggered","rather","decision","same","time","happens","itself","becomes","trigger","progress","visibility","research","amabile","kramer","single","motivator","perceived","harder","reducing","session","